t each coupon row contributes one observation, and applies scipy.stats.ttest_ind with pooled variance yielding t(46), i.e., 24 rows per arm treated as independent although each arm contains only 6 independent plates with 4 repeated coupons each.\",\"The reported degrees of freedom (46) correspond to 48 independent rows; under the declared plate_id unit only 12 independent units exist (df = 10 at plate level), so the row-independent procedure entered repeated measurements from the same unit as independent, and no aggregation to plate level or clustering adjustment appears anywhere in the workflow or report.\",\"The minted lock's authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly [\\\"plate_id\\\"], matching the declared independent-unit column in data-description.md, with authority explicitly limited to the case, input digest, procedure and ordered key and claiming no numerical or scientific correctness.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declared independent-unit column plate_id is consistent with the frozen data: 12 distinct plate labels each appear exactly 4 times (one per coupon slot A-D), and build_orientation is constant within each plate, so plates nest cleanly into the two procedure arms (6 flat plates, 6 edge plates).","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it reports 48 coupon rows from only 12 distinct build plates, states that each coupon row contributes one observation, and applies scipy.stats.ttest_ind with pooled variance yielding t(46), i.e., 24 rows per arm treated as independent although each arm contains only 6 independent plates with 4 repeated coupons each.","The reported degrees of freedom (46) correspond to 48 independent rows; under the declared plate_id unit only 12 independent units exist (df = 10 at plate level), so the row-independent procedure entered repeated measurements from the same unit as independent, and no aggregation to plate level or clustering adjustment appears anywhere in the workflow or report.","The minted lock's authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly [\"plate_id\"], matching the declared independent-unit column in data-description.md, with authority explicitly limited to the case, input digest, procedure and ordered key and claiming no numerical or scientific correctness."]},"ttft_ms":7422,"ttft_stream_ms":1504,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":15490,"uuid":"f8b9f844-d367-4b42-b82c-50940348cbc8"}
